      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes a lot of sense for the social democratic side. it feels like a really robust ethical framework. can you do the same for the libertarian side? i need to make sure i'm not underselling them. could you get into the actual philosophical foundations of their argument against taxation/redistribution? i'm looking for something more sophisticated than just 'it's stealing'—like the deeper moral arguments regarding self-ownership or the role of the state.",
